ecause it didn't really capture  any of my personality it was really just  me staring blankly at the phone and it  didn't have any of the normal like  friendly affectations that I would have  if you're talking to me directly and I  thought maybe that they also said this  because they had never seen me without  makeup on before uh which  accounted for most of the clips that  were in this project because a lot of  them uh were from when I was at home  and also if you're wondering uh yes did  uh did the app really change the way  that I used my phone it really did  um at this time and I allowed this to  happen so it was really hard to tell  what felt like it was authentic and what  didn't I did not try to perform for the  camera but there were some things where  I would catch myself wondering would I  do this if I wasn't recording or  do I not want to do this because I'm  recording and is that okay and do I know  now am I thinking too hard about it  should I stop doing it anyway or  whatever uh but I did use my phone a lot  less during this time which in some ways  was really good for me but in other ways  I had turned turned my phone into this  uh awful kind of recording device so  that had its own uh things with it and  the other major uh change was that I  rarely ever took my phone into the  bathroom during this specific period of  time  uh and here's the same project installed  in another location at the San Francisco  museum of modern modern art and so the  work was up for about three months there  and I had an opportunity to watch people  take their own posed selfies in front of  the work and sometimes they'd find me on  Instagram and actually tag me in these  selfies uh or mention me which was uh  really special and while it seems like  the project is really exposing and it is  um because all of these videos are  playing back simultaneously it's also  really dizzying and so it feels like  it's also a place to hide it's hard to  focus on any one clip because it's